item 1 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/1/measure".

item 1 measure is an assessment statement.

item 1 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 1 measure has the judgement "The European Business Wallets will build on and extend the ecosystem of trust established under the European Digital Identity Framework, established by Regulation (EU) 910/2014 on electronic identification and trust services for electronic transactions in the internal market, as amended by Regulation (EU) 2024/118318 (including adopted implementing acts).
Providers of the European Business wallets must comply with the requirements of Directive (EU) 2022/2555 (NIS2) of the European Parliament and of the Council on measures for a high common level of cybersecurity across the Union. Likewise, the European Digital Directory shall be operated in alignment with the principles enshrined under NIS2.
Cryptographic operators or other operations processing critical assets shall be performed in accordance with the requirements for the characteristics and design of electronic identification means at assurance level substantial as set out in Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2015/1502.
The European Data Protection Supervisor were consulted in accordance with Article 42(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725.
The proposal anticipates that the European Business Wallets should also enable the exchange of attestations for the purpose of delegating digital power of attorney, as established by Directive (EU) 2025/25, allowing economic operators and public sector bodies to exchange attestations with their Business Wallets to delegate authority to representatives.".

item 1 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeAlignmentMeasure".

item 1 measure has the description "Alignmentwith existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified".

item 1 measure has the title "European Business Wallet".


item 2 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/2/measure".

item 2 measure is an assessment statement.

item 2 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 2 measure has the judgement "In each Member State, the supervisory bodies designated pursuant to Article 46a of Regulation (EU) No 910/2014 shall also be the supervisory bodies for the purposes of this Regulation. The Regulation provides for the role and tasks of such authorities.
Member States shall ensure that the supervisory bodies referred to in paragraph 1 possess the necessary powers and adequate resources for the exercise of their tasks in an effective, efficient, and independent manner.
Where a Union entity is a provider of European Business Wallets the Commission shall be the responsible supervisory body.".

item 2 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure".

item 2 measure has the description "Organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen".

item 2 measure has the title "European Business Wallet".


item 3 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/3/measure".

item 3 measure is an assessment statement.

item 3 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 3 measure has the judgement "EBW owner identification data shall be issued in a format according to one of the standards listed in Annex II of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2979 and as QEAA or EAA depending on the issuing entity.
The annexes define the high-level requirements that will be then instantiated in specifications and standards in the upcoming implementing act to ensure a shared understanding of the data.
Business Wallets shall support the secure export and portability of an owner’s European Business Wallet data in at least an open format.".

item 3 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeSharedMeasure".

item 3 measure has the description "Measures taken to ensure a shared understanding of the dataPlease list such measures".

item 3 measure has the title "European Business Wallet".


item 4 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/4/measure".

item 4 measure is an assessment statement.

item 4 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 4 measure has the judgement "Adopt implementing acts for the definition of reference standards and specifications.".

item 4 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeStandardsMeasure".

item 4 measure has the description "Use of commonly agreed open technical specifications and standardsPlease list such measures".

item 4 measure has the title "European Business Wallet".


item 5 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/5/measure".

item 5 measure is an assessment statement.

item 5 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 5 measure has the judgement "Alignment ensured for the European Business Wallets, as detailed above.".

item 5 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeAlignmentMeasure".

item 5 measure has the description "Alignmentwith existing digital and sectorial policiesPlease list the applicable digital and sectorial policies identified".

item 5 measure has the title "Digital public services in Member States that are mandated to receive evidence through European Business Wallets".


item 6 measure is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/assessment/1/6/measure".

item 6 measure is an assessment statement.

item 6 measure has for "cav:interpretation" the resource "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#InterpretationPositive".

item 6 measure has the judgement "Article 15 mandates Member States to enable economic operators to exchange information with public sector bodies via the European Business Wallet.".

item 6 measure has the statement type "http://data.europa.eu/leg/interop-assessment#StatementTypeOrganisationMeasure".

item 6 measure has the description "Organisational measures for a smooth cross-border digital public services deliveryPlease list the governance measures foreseen".

item 6 measure has the title "Digital public services in Member States that are mandated to receive evidence through European Business Wallets".


